    {
      "id": "claim_17facb32525648bf858a6b8838ee921d",
      "statement": "On 2024-05-31 (month-end), Wire Status Lite pilot polling (60 clients, browser refresh every 30 seconds per visible wire) combined with production wire-release status refreshes drove approximately 85 TPS against the PPH v1 status API, exhausting its thread pool and delaying wire release 47 minutes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/pir-2024-07-wire-status-lite-pilot-inc-2024-1182-post-implementation-review.md#L24-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:47c1705db6ff961019a77cb29b6253eeb8c9aac385661d336843d74208a8cabd:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3c84ee3cbbfd472591448040e616d680",
      "statement": "INC-2024-1182 impact included 1,240 wires delayed, 312 wires released after the 6:00 p.m. ET Fedwire customer cutoff requiring next-day value, and compensation of $41,800 to 14 clients for interest claims; no regulatory notification was required because no data was exposed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/pir-2024-07-wire-status-lite-pilot-inc-2024-1182-post-implementation-review.md#L28-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fe074407839fd331189b7b2809338c4ee513b6e599547aa968351919c79a00a8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d83cf0e027ea4a58b35310bacb10f725",
      "statement": "PIR-2024-07 identified three root causes for INC-2024-1182: a polling architecture against a shared synchronous API with no client-side backoff, no capacity test at month-end volumes, and status semantics that were not validated with Compliance or Legal before client exposure.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/pir-2024-07-wire-status-lite-pilot-inc-2024-1182-post-implementation-review.md#L45-L51",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9e71d2f93a360cfa2460e517259613f7b7db12d400b3196ac826dd19f447e343:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e80127f00b46422fac9669897049c529",
      "statement": "Corrective actions from INC-2024-1182 were: rate-limiting the PPH v1 status API to 20 TPS shared (done 2024-06, owner PPH), adopting an event-driven status pattern that became ADR-PAY-019 (done 2024-06, owner Enterprise Architecture), building a reusable CBO status projection service (delivered for ACH in 2025 via CBO-3815), and validating client-facing status terminology with FCC and Legal before future tracking features (left open, carried forward).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://sources/estate/pir-2024-07-wire-status-lite-pilot-inc-2024-1182-post-implementation-review.md#L53-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:48e33e8afd5d89a9891ca2815cbb357d002f93967de9d8394a7e0632cdb08305:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7e07a03cf3764f0ea9a35ff810881a24",
      "statement": "The Wire Status Lite pilot (CBO-3120) was closed as 'Won't Do' as a direct result of being the cause of INC-2024-1182, and this closure plus the incident are documented together in PIR-2024-07.",
